ADIB's EGP7,550,833 thousand consolidated total profit converts by dividing by 1,000 to EGP7,550.833 million. ORAS reports USD127.8 million consolidated total profit directly. Both concern six months ended 30 June 2026; matching dates and the word million do not make the currencies or economic scopes interchangeable. Neither a direct numeric ranking nor a raw sum is meaningful.

A common-currency comparison needs a disclosed, period-appropriate FX translation basis. Even after translation, total group profit includes NCI; investor comparisons require consistent owner attribution, capital employed, risk and market valuation. Bank profits depend on deposit/financing spreads, provisioning and regulatory capital. Construction profits depend on project margins, billing/collections and working capital. The positive profits are supportive observations, but the ADIB page lacks loan-quality detail and the ORAS profit page alone cannot demonstrate cash realization. I would not declare either company cheaper or superior from absolute profit size. Obtain FX inputs, comparable owner earnings, balance-sheet/cash-quality information and current corporate-action-adjusted valuations. The bounded conclusion is two correctly labeled historical earnings observations, suitable for separate sector analysis, with no allocation ranking or trade clearance.
